From e4e0e66e9d60166d530b2080f968d3999d3bab8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 16:21:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/mediatek: transfer inherited MT6897 DMA power ownership

An IOMMU probe reference keeps the M4U powered but does not own the larbs
or OVL clocks. The translated handover can release its temporary OVL/larb
references before the first CRTC takes persistent references, leaving live
bootloader scanout without a complete owner.

Add a built-in independent boot owner that acquires both physical larb
paths and the clock of every represented OVL before component registration.
Require the GCE managed resume and synchronous suspend qualification before
acknowledging either fabric guard. A failed STOP restores its consumed PM
reference and retains the quarantine; another normal GCE user keeps its own
reference. Require built-in GCE and runtime PM for this contract.

Validate the complete engine set and the source-defined non-fetching state
of OVL7 and POSTMASKs before acknowledging both initial IOMMU guards.
Acquisition failure retains only resources actually acquired; a failure
before any acquisition remains retryable. Component probe/bind errors do
not destroy inherited leases.

Transfer each active engine lease only after successful full CRTC setup
or the normal stop sequence while ordinary PM/clock references are held.
The existing last-user larb sleep acknowledgment remains the DMA drain
boundary and preserves upstream references on failure. Keep the helper
built in, with manual unbind disabled, so quarantined state survives DRM
component failure and cannot disappear with a removable DRM module.

Give firmware-bank initialization its own balanced PM reference and expose
an idempotent, provider-locked boot-guard acknowledgment API. Add address-mode
independent OVL supplier links, preserving existing translated attachments.

The register predicates and OVL3 larb1/larb0 mapping follow the pinned
MediaTek mtk_disp_ovl.c, mtk_disp_postmask.c and mt6897.dts sources.

Link: https://github.com/MiCode/MTK_kernel_device_modules/tree/3c4ccd07d5624879555ec710c11bb8818e5cb5c6
Signed-off-by: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/Kconfig              |  11 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/Makefile             |   2 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_crtc.c           |   8 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_ddp_comp.c       |   1 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_ddp_comp.h       |   7 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_disp_boot.c      | 411 ++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_disp_boot.h      |  20 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_disp_drv.h       |   1 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_disp_ovl.c       |  28 ++
 drivers/iommu/mtk_iommu.c                     |  60 ++-
 drivers/memory/mtk-smi.c                      |   9 +
 include/soc/mediatek/mtk_iommu.h              |  14 +
 include/soc/mediatek/smi.h                    |  10 +
 tools/testing/selftests/mtk_display/Makefile  |   3 +
 .../mtk_display/test_boot_ownership.py        | 190 ++++++++
 .../selftests/mtk_display/test_iommu_guard.py |  74 ++++
 .../selftests/mtk_vcp/test_smi_suppliers.py   |   5 +-
 17 files changed, 841 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)
